when a bag is made from a billboard it  has a story its creative its bold every  bag is giving back and it's being  eco-friendly I was working advertising  and I saw that all the billboards that  were going up in essence we're going to  the landfill most people don't know that  billboards are made of vinyl and it can  be turned into something else and so  let's create a business that's solely  based on billboards on any given month  we get close to around 10,000 pounds of  billboards that we turn into product  once that billboard goes up it's usually  up for a period of about 4 weeks is what  a typical campaign is on the street for  its then shipped to our facility here we  sort it we cut it and send it to the  manufacturer or where they do the final  sewing and cleaning of the product we're  able to take a billboard that had one  purpose and then reuse it to make  something else my brother myself are  both huge surfers and we kind of felt  like the sort of community loves bright  colors and billboard vinyl is actually  very durable it's a thick material it's  waterproof its milder proof so it's  actually the perfect material for a  surfboard back after that we spent in  two backpacks duffle bags wallets fanny  packs hip packs snowboard bags every  products different every products  one-of-a-kind each piece that we make is  unlike anything before it  our playground for all of us is based in  the environment whether it's the  mountains the rivers the the ocean it's  something that we in essence have a  responsibility to maintain and sustain
 

